        "Training: ▶ Start workout and the calendar are at the top. The client's alerts (recovery check, foundation program to approve, injury check, pre-start form, exercises that hurt) sit under one line, 🔔 3 things to check; tap it to open them. It only shows when there's something. Open 🎥 Form videos to watch their videos (new ones are marked) and write your correction under the video while it plays; tap Watch again to replay it. Put workouts on their calendar (if they're on the Health Reset, the app warns you and shows which week they're on), switch Gym/Home, and see their training log. Programs only go on the calendar now: a client still on an old-style program shows it under ⚙️ More options, with its extra cardio and Take off. For home clients, 🏠 Home equipment shows what they own, with photos; tap Edit on a multi station to load the exercises it can do. The app then picks home exercises their equipment covers, and you can still change any of them. Gold stars show where they improved.",
        "🩹 Injury check: after you pick any program or workout, a sign pops up. It checks exercise names against the client's injuries (their injury list, which the intake form now asks about, and open pain reports). It's a name check, not a clinical assessment, so use your own judgement. No clashes found means nothing matched. Otherwise it shows how many exercises to check: tap Take me to each one, and each opens in amber with the injury it may affect and 3 other options. Swap it, or tap Keep it anyway and give a reason (lighter load, shorter range...). Injuries from the intake form can be marked healed like any other.",
        "😣 Exercises that hurt: when a client taps This hurts during a workout, you get a push and the exercise shows under the injury check with where it hurt and what they tried instead. For a shoulder it offers the same movement at a kinder angle or grip (overhead → incline → flat press, wide grip → neutral grip). To change it for good, tap the exercise in their program or on a calendar day.",
        "📅 The calendar shows one week at a time, Monday to Sunday, like the client's: each day with its workout and session in gold, mobility and flexibility in teal, stability in purple and recovery in green. Tap ‹ › to change week. Tap a day to see its details: extra blocks you added show ✅ Done or ⚠️ Couldn't do it once the client taps it.",
        "📅 Setting up a program (on the Training tab, right under Start workout): tap the day the client starts, choose A whole program, pick their goal (Build muscle, Get stronger, Fat loss, Fitness, Sport, Mobility & flexibility, 60+ Longevity or Rehab). The program that fits their level from the intake form shows first with a ⭐; tap it, or another one under it, then tap the days the client trains (the program's own days are ticked to start with; Sunday is always rest) and tap Activate program. The whole program goes on, spread over those days: fewer days just takes more weeks, and a yellow note says how long and where its easy weeks land. If the client trains on different days each week, tap week 1's days and choose 🎲 Different days each week (or 🔁 Same days every week): Go ahead then asks which days the next week is on, and the program carries on in order. Week 1 goes on the calendar. When the client has 2 workouts left, you get a notification and a card above their calendar: tap ✅ Go ahead to add the next week, or make changes first (tap any exercise to swap it or change sets and reps) if they're struggling, it's too easy or they have a problem. If the client already has workouts in those weeks (say you're adding stretching, mobility or rehab to their training), choose Add it alongside: their workouts stay and the new session goes under the workout on days they share, so they can do more than one thing a day. Replace takes the old workouts off. Tap any day after to change that one workout. 🧘 To put a running stability program on the calendar, tap a day and choose Put it on this day, or Every (weekday) until it ends; stability days show in purple with a ✓ once logged. Form videos, other exercise, recovery, where they train, the training log and more options are under the tap-to-open headings below the calendar.",
        "📅 Training calendar: you don't have to give a whole program either. Tap a day, choose One workout and pick any workout, or open a weekly program and pick one of its days, so you can mix and match, like a gym day on Monday, mobility on Tuesday, gym again on Wednesday and flexibility on Thursday. When the workouts are ready, tap Save and tell (right under the calendar) and the client gets a notification that their workout is loaded. If you change their workouts and leave the client without tapping it, the app asks whether to send it or leave without sending. Tap ＋ Add a block to put an extra block (mobility, flexibility or a fight session) on the same day, to suit the client and their energy. Take it off removes a block.",
        "Tap any exercise in their program or calendar to swap it or change the sets and reps, for this client only.",
