        "🏋️ My workout (Menu ☰ → My workout, or Profile > My training → Start my workout): tap it to log your own training. The same live workout screen opens for you: pick any exercise, log your sets, weights and effort, or tap ⚡ Do a superset, then tap Finish workout. Your last two weeks and your progress graphs show under the button. You never show on your Clients tab or count as a client.",
        "👥 Group live session (next to Start live session): train up to 4 clients at once on your phone. Tick who's training; each person gets their own colour and letter (A, B, C, D) for the whole session. Run one client's workout for today or build it as you go with + Add an exercise. For each exercise, tap a person's card to log their set: the box shows their name in their colour and the button says Save (name)'s set. Tapped the wrong person? Tap Wrong person? under their last set to move it. For a superset, tap ⚡ Do a superset, tick 2-4 exercises in order and tap Start: each person's card then logs their whole round (weight, reps and effort for each exercise) in one go. Tap End superset to go back to one exercise at a time. Tap Finish group session and each person's sets save to their own profile as a 🤝 in-person session.",
        "🌳 Longevity programs: when you put one on the calendar, pick Start at which block? Block 1 (weeks 1-8), 2 (weeks 9-16) or 3 (weeks 17-24). Pick the next block when the client is ready to progress, or the same block again to repeat it. 📅 Muscle Year programs work the same way with four 13-week blocks (weeks 1-13, 14-26, 27-39 and 40-52).",
        "🎯 Gauge test: the first time a client does an exercise, their first set is a gauge set at a weight they pick, stopping 1-2 reps short. The app works out their working weight from it, and their training log marks it 🎯 Gauge set. Full explanation in ☰ → Coaching guides → Training each body part → Gauge test, so you can explain it to them.",
        "🌙 Deload weeks (above the calendar on the Training tab): the app watches each client's training. After about 6 weeks in a row with 2 or more workouts, or sooner when they show signs of fatigue (lots of sets to failure, tired days, poor sleep, missed workouts, no improvements), you get a notification and a Time for a deload week card. Pick when it starts (next Monday, the Monday after, or tomorrow): that week they do the same workouts with half the sets at about 70% of the weight, and everything on the calendar from that day moves back one week, so their program carries straight on after. Deload days show as 🌙 Deload on the calendar. Let the client know it's coming. You can add one any time from the small Deload line. Programs with their own easy weeks (the 12-week programs, the Muscle Year programs, the 8-week sports, fight and off-season programs) count those as deloads, so the card says one is coming instead of asking you to add another.",
        "🏃 Other exercise (Training tab): walks, runs, rides, hikes, swims and sport the client logged outside their program in the last 7 days, with time, distance, pace and average heart rate. Long or hard sessions count as training load in their recovery suggestions and daily summary. Ones marked ⌚ watch came in by themselves from their watch.",
